+## 1. What this experiment can establish
+
+The independent path can observe one checked RESET/base/setup/first-RUN/clock/PAUSE sequence, ending before any software FIFO data-port access. It neither includes nor calls the old ID/initializer cores (K:9–32,408–468; A:23–51,120,163–165). **No new FIFO words/tags/ID call is a software-scope fact; physical I2C silence is unverified.** First RUN may resume retained FIFO/parser activity or another owner's work. Zero observed FIFO counters, OP full-bit changes, returned reset writes, and VALID+RESET do not settle that question (K:24–42; P:54–60).
+
+Source-supported ordering is SW_RESET → checked RESET → ordinary STATE RESET → base CONFIG/ERREN/mask/master → FIFO count/mode setup in RESET → first RUN → divider → PAUSE. C:265–295,299–390,667–685,710–724,1870–1903 supports these components and their relative placement, not the entire diagnostic's exact 18-write list or its safety on this board. R30 deliberately inserts extra observations and freezes before vendor FIFO preload/second RUN.
+
+## 2. Shared predicates and measurement meaning
+
+- Each named snapshot attempts **two passes × 17 registers** in S:63–80 order. `pass0=pass1=0x0001ffff` plus `complete=1` means 34 accepted reads, **not** predicate admission, physical certification, or an atomic snapshot. A result always prints 272 field records; unreached/invalid records explicitly say `valid=0 value=unread` and must not be counted as measurements (K:93–104,265–286; A:139–158; S:148–205).
+- `pre` requires exact equality between both passes. Later captures permit only OPERATIONAL bits 6/7 (`0xc0`) to vary between passes; the raw `stable`/`changed` masks still report that difference. If OP alone differs, `stable=0x1ffef`, `changed=0x10` can be admissible; this is not an all-fields-stable result (K:279–285; S:167–169).
+- Every non-pre admission requires VERSION `0x20060000`, raw ERROR_FLAGS `0`, exact I2C_STATUS `0x0c000000`, and OP containing **only** bits 6/7. Bits 4/5 and 8–13 (`0x3f30`) stop as activity; bits outside `0x3ff0` stop as unknown. Admissible raw OP is therefore `0`, `0x40`, `0x80`, or `0xc0`, without assigning full-bit occupancy/permission semantics (K:66–77,295–308).
+- STATE must have VALID bit2, the phase's low state 0/1/3, and opaque remainder `(STATE & ~0x17)` equal to `0` or `0x108`. This excludes FLUSH bit6 and state2. Bits in `0x108` are an observed envelope, not source-defined capability. From base onward master-generation bit4 is required separately (K:289–292,314–345; H:71–84).
+- Fresh single-pass guards reread all 17 fields, STATE last, before mutation stages. These are serialized observations; they cannot make a whole write batch or hardware ownership atomic (K:358–368,423–453).
+
+## 3. Eight phases and exact admission predicates
+
+The following counts refer to the **full-path write prefix at that capture**, not proof that a capture was reached. Any shorter prefix is possible when a callback/guard stops inside a batch.
+
+| Phase | Write prefix | Additional predicates, beyond the shared rules | What a stop does and does not imply |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `pre` | 0 | Both passes and a fresh guard exactly match: VERSION `20060000`, STATE `11c`, CONFIG `0`, IO `a5`, OP `c0`, ERROR `0`, ERREN `3c`, OPMASK `0`, six counts `0`, MASTER `0`, CLK `0`, STATUS `0c000000` (K:144–148,317–321,423–426). | Signature/stability mismatch blocks this core's first reset write. It does not diagnose the owner, target chip, or actual FIFO occupancy. |
+| `post_reset` | 1 | After sole SW_RESET and VALID+RESET polling: STATE low0; IO with PACK/UNPACK bits removed equals `a5`; both FIFO counters and all four MX counters `0`; CLK `0`; CONFIG `0`; MASTER `0/1`; ERREN `0/3c`; OPMASK `0/300` (K:325–340,426–428). Master-generation is not required yet. | Reset was requested if traced. A mismatch may violate conservative policy; it does not establish failed internal reset. No base writes follow failed admission. |
+| `base` | 6 | Ordinary STATE RESET was checked before writes 3–6. VALID+RESET+master-generation; CONFIG `207`, MASTER `1`, ERREN `3c`, OPMASK `300`; IO geometry `a5` with PACK/UNPACK optional; all six counts `0`, CLK `0` (K:325–345,430–434). | Source-shaped base admission is incomplete/failed. A base flag0 may coexist with some/all base writes; use trace, not flags, for issued writes. ERREN `3c` enables core error sources. |
+| `setup` | 15 | VALID+RESET+master-generation; CONFIG `207`, MASTER `1`, ERREN `0`, mask `300`, IO **exactly `c0a5`**; OUT/IN FIFO counts `0`, MX_OUTPUT/MX_INPUT `0`, MX_READ **3**, MX_WRITE **9**; CLK `0` (K:327–345,436–439). | Setup not admitted. Nonzero 3/9 are intentional aggregate byte counts, not FIFO occupancy or a sent transaction. No first RUN follows a failed setup gate. |
+| `run` | 16 | Same configured fields/counts as setup, STATE low1 VALID+master-generation, CLK still `0`; transition polling accepts only low state0 or1 and the known envelope (K:371–395,441–444). | Write16 may already have entered RUN even if `run_observed=0`. Activity/status/error before own tags is unexpected evidence, not an ID response. No cleanup PAUSE/RESET is attempted on this failure. |
+| `clock` | 17 | Preserve checked RUN/setup fields and counts; CLK **`003e007c`**, with exact readback (K:334–345,446–449). | Divider may have been written before a flag0/stop. It is a MiCode nominal100kHz choice, not a measured SCL frequency or confirmation of stock-board rate (C:408–456,461–470). |
+| `pause` | 18 | Preserve clock/setup fields/counts; STATE low3 VALID+master-generation; transition accepts only low1 or3 (K:371–395,451–455). | PAUSE request is not PAUSE observation. Even a passed gate leaves raw full-bit/ownership semantics unresolved. No FIFO data, second RUN, or cleanup reset follows. |
+| `terminal` | existing prefix | If no earlier failure, requires the same predicates as pause and successful pair capture. If already logically stopped, it is **capture only**: the `!w.failed` short circuit skips terminal predicate admission. Poisoned I/O/time/cap paths skip capture entirely (K:456–463). | An early-stop terminal may show RESET/RUN/other state; do not relabel it PAUSE. Only full success yields `observed/prefifo_pause_observed_no_new_tags`. `terminal_gic=unread` remains explicit (A:163–171). |
+
+**Source versus policy:** source definitions support low STATE values/VALID/master-generation, register addresses, CONFIG mini-core2/N7, FIFO versus block counts and PACK/UNPACK (H:43–125,144–147; C:299–390). Exact inherited values, VERSION/STATE-aux envelope, all-counts-zero reset/base admission, exact idle status, 64-byte geometry restriction, strict readback and rejection of all raw errors/activity are **conservative R30 policy**. There is no architectural reset-value table proving them necessary on every valid device. Setup intentionally changes counters to3/9. R30 keeps OPMASK `300` and changes ERREN to0, whereas vendor FIFO setup normally unmasks services; this is an explicit polling adaptation, not literal stock behavior (K:21–42,311–347; C:382–388; P:25,31,35–58).
