+Logical first failure remains sticky; if not poisoned, a **read-only** terminal capture may still be attempted. A later terminal fault can add failed-access evidence without replacing the original reason. `failure valid=0 access=unread off=unread` only means no recorded failed/late core read/write; it does not certify absence of policy stops (K:150–159,188–195,456–463; A:134–138).
