+## 8. STATUS decoding, R29 comparison and bounded recommendation
+
+The later terminal status has **zero intersection with both named error masks**, MiCode ISR `0x0380003c` and broader MiCode-header/Linux `0x038000fc` (H:127–171; C:1718–1741; L:113–117,288–307). ERROR_FLAGS is also0. At those terminal samples BUS_ACTIVEbit8/BUS_MASTERbit9/WR_BUFFER_FULLbit0/NACKbit3/ARB_LOSTbit4 are0 and sampled SDA/SCL bits26/27 are high. These sampled predicates do not exclude transient traffic or establish physical silence/ownership.
+
+**No exact field names or code meanings for STATUS bits16/20 are established by the obtained fixed sources.** They are unnamed in H/C and L; H:174–178 only names two clock-state values without a field extraction, and H:622/645 references a separate `i2c-msm-v2-debug` implementation. A bounded workspace filename search including ignored files found no such implementation. No network fetch or alternative unpinned source was used. Therefore this analysis does not invent OUT/IN/CLK FSM labels or call the values benign. The immediate software stop is a **conservative whole-register equality mismatch**, not evidence of a named error, NACK, or chip nonresponse.
+
+R29 stopped before first RUN at the custom OP-zero gate, with six writes, STATE11c/OPc0/STATUS old idle, IOa5 and all counts0 (R29:22–46,62–68). R30 reproduces the same inherited signature and first six write values, admits setup with9/3 aggregate counts and PACK/UNPACK, then issues first RUN before stopping. The terminal changes provide a new state-dependent observation; they do not settle the meaning of FULL flags or reset effect. CLK0 remains before its unissued programming stage and does not alone diagnose a clock fault.
+
+**Recommendation for a separately reviewed future host revision:** keep the frozen, consumed R30 unchanged. First retain the **failing transition poll's raw VERSION/ERROR/STATUS/OP/STATE, timestamp and from/target/phase** before evaluating its predicate, without another MMIO read or hidden cleanup/retry. Obtain the pinned MiCode debug field masks and value tables before considering a **phase-aware** RUN/CLK/PAUSE status policy; preserve raw bits and explicit known-error/activity/line/unreviewed-bit guards. Do not simply mask bits16/20, drop status checks, or extend this result into CLK/FIFO/ID permission. Existing source-supported RUN→CLK→PAUSE ordering is not itself a board-level safety certificate.
+
+Unknowns remain: raw/time of the first failed poll; precise bits16/20 semantics; reset internal effect/hidden FIFO-parser state/count-read side effects; exclusive owner/electrical state/transient bus activity; terminal GIC; physical return screen. Divider/PAUSE, ID/ACK, IRQ/HID and physical touch were not exercised. **No success, physical bus-silence, ownership, controller-ID, new device operation or automatic retry claim is made.**
